  "ingredients": [
    "4 cup broccoli (~10 ounces)",
    "1 1/2 cup almond flour",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon paprika",
    "1 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1/2 teaspoon baking soda",
    "2 large egg",
    "1/4 cup coconut oil",
    "4 1/2 ounce cheddar cheese (shredded)",
    "1/2 teaspoon apple cider vinegar"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375F. Once done, measure out the broccoli florets.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105189.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Put the broccoli florets into a food processor. If you don't have a food processor, I recommend the one I use - it lasts a long time and it's really cheap considering how useful it is.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105190.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pulse your broccoli florets in the food processor until it's finely chopped. I do this in small batches, remove the broccoli, then add more to the food processor.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105192.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a large mixing bowl, add almond flour, salt, paprika, garlic powder, pepper, and baking soda.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105193.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the spices and almond flour together, then add eggs and coconut oil (or melted butter).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105194.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the eggs and oil (or butter) together with the almond flour until a dough forms.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105195.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add broccoli to the mixture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105197.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine everything well using your hands.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105198.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grate cheddar cheese. I grate my own cheese now, because you will find excess carbs from pre-shredded cheese. They normally coat the cheese with corn starch so that it doesn't stick together.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105200.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add cheese to the dough.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105201.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix together everything with your hands again, until the cheese is evenly distributed throughout.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105202.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Put your nonstick silpat on a cookie sheet, so that they don't stick as they cook. Form patties out of the dough.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105204.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake the biscuits for 12-15 minutes or until they start to get flattened.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105207.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using a spoon and your fingers, mold the flattened biscuits into a more biscuit like shape. Add some contours and texture around them.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105209.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue baking for about 5 minutes. Then, turn your oven to broil and broil the biscuits for 3-5 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-14",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105211.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let the biscuits cool for 2-3 minutes, then remove them from your silpat and place them on a cooling rack. Cool for 5-10 minutes and serve!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-broccoli-cheddar-biscuits/#wprm-recipe-50821-step-0-15",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/P2105214.jpg"
    }
  ],
